What are fixtures?

Fixtures are reusuable functions that prepares the environmants needed for a testcase(s) and optionally cleans up after execution is done

eg;opening a browser , connecting to db. So basically it is a setup and clean up mechanism 

Imagine a cricket match.

Before the players start playing:

The pitch is prepared.
The stumps are fixed.
The ball is brought.
The scoreboard is reset.
The umpires are ready.

The players don't prepare these things themselves—they simply come and play.

A fixture is like the ground staff. It prepares everything before the match and cleans up afterward.

Similarly, in Playwright:

Launch the browser
Open a page
Log in (if required)

The test only focuses on verifying functionality.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why do we use fixtures?

Fixtures provide several benefits:

♻️ Code reuse – Write setup once, use it in many tests.
🧹 Cleaner tests – Test functions contain only test logic.
🔧 Easy maintenance – Update setup in one place.
⚡ Consistent environment – Every test starts from a known state.
